From: Dastano <197081+Dastano@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:16:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 67/67] shadow: helpers woken at a submission's start
 (VICTORY_PASSES_HOT)

While a submission is prepared, the copy helpers are woken at its start
and an idle one waits awake for the next pass, up to VICTORY_PASSES_HOT
microseconds after the last work (0, the default: off, as before),
yielding now and then. A pass then finds them awake and the waking
overlaps the submission's asking. foxhound's launcher sets 1 (woken at
each start, asleep soon after): the longest frame walking went from 525
to 145 ms (RTX 4090, Ryzen 9 7950X3D). Longer values spin cores and hurt
when threads outnumber cores.

From readmet3xt-lab/foxhound 0.2.0-pre.4 (PR #13 by Dastano).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01G6tkVHCftUUQbGm5NirGaG
